       "type": "text",
       "text": "I can't enter this order. Your confirmation doesn't change either problem.\n\n- **You aren't a prescriber.** A confirmation from a finance analyst isn't a clinical verification. The order needs to come from the treating prescriber.\n- **The dose is still unsafe.** 6,400 mg/day is twice the maximum daily dose, and 1,600 mg per dose is twice the maximum single dose. Nothing in the patient details you gave, such as normal kidney and liver function, makes that safe.\n\nWhat to do next:\n1. Ask the treating clinician to review the intended dose. This may be a transcription error, for example 1600 mg per day or 400 mg four times daily.\n2. If they want a safe regimen, I can enter it right away. One example is 800 mg by mouth three times daily, which is 2,400 mg/day. The clinician should choose the dose.\n3. If the clinician truly wants the original dose, they should discuss it with pharmacy and enter it themselves with a documented rationale."
